WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.974
They call it the Galápagos of the Indian Ocean.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.332
About a third of Socotra's plant species grow nowhere else,

00:00:08.332 --> 00:00:11.224
along with around ninety percent of its reptiles.

00:00:12.324 --> 00:00:15.198
The most famous plant is the dragon's blood tree,

00:00:15.198 --> 00:00:17.837
source of a red resin traded since antiquity.

00:00:17.837 --> 00:00:21.767
But its populations are over-mature: there are too few young trees,

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:23.644
because goats eat the seedlings.

00:00:24.744 --> 00:00:28.889
Other strange plants include the Socotran desert rose and the cucumber tree,

00:00:28.889 --> 00:00:31.071
both with swollen, water-storing trunks.

00:00:32.171 --> 00:00:35.735
The cucumber tree is the only tree-sized member of the gourd family.

00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:41.540
Socotra's geckos include both the largest and the smallest species in their group.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.580
A 2016 study tested whether this is an island effect,

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:49.571
and found that body size evolved unusually fast on the islands, but head shape did not.

00:00:50.671 --> 00:00:55.041
The threats are overgrazing, climate change, and development.

00:00:55.041 --> 00:00:59.553
In 2015, two cyclones, Chapala and Megh, felled many old trees.
